<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Karakalpak Autonomous Oblast</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1925–1932</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Karakalpak Autonomous Oblast was a Soviet territory created in 1925 in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oxus">Amu Darya</a> delta for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karakalpaks">Karakalpaks</a>, from lands of the former Khorezm People's Soviet Republic. It was first attached to the Kazakh ASSR. In 1932 it became the Karakalpak ASSR, which was transferred to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzbeks">Uzbek</a> SSR in 1936 and is now Karakalpakstan in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uzbekistan">Uzbekistan</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/karakalpak-autonomous-oblast.jpg" alt="Karakalpak Autonomous Oblast" width="320" height="211" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fotisgrek · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Russian_SFSR_-_Karakalpak_(1930.07.20).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
